<title>USA: ABN AMRO unit's Chicago Corp buy approved.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO unit's Chicago Corp buy approved.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO Holding NV said Thursday the Federal Reserve Board approved the purchase of Chicago Corp by its ABN AMRO North America Inc subsidiary.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO said it will merge the Chicago investment bank with ABN AMRO North America's securities unit to form ABN AMRO Chicago Corp.</p>
<p>ABN AMRO is the world's 14th largest bank with assets of more than $385 billion. ABN AMRO has assets of more than $72 billion in North America</p>
<p>The deal will close January 2, ABN AMRO said.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
